/* Classic (0.97) look for the generic confirm dialog (CGenericConfirmDialog): the stone box of the
   in-game confirmations (RenderMessageBox 0051af50, codes 0x97 / 0x99: selling a dear item,
   combining, a changed trade, a split server, using a fruit) and of the personal-code keypad
   (FUN_004eb070). The box is Message_box2 (213x5) as the top edge, N strips of Message_box1
   (213x40, the stone with its golden sides) and Message_box2 again as the bottom edge, 213 wide
   at x 213 with its top at y 100 of the 640x480 frame: 213x130 (three strips) for a
   confirmation, 213x170 (four) for the keypad. OK is Ok / Ok2 and Cancel is Cancel / Cancel2
   (70x21, the second image under the mouse) at (234, 190) and (333, 190): 21 and 120 from the
   box's left, 90 from its top. The lines are bold, 18 apart from y 130, golden (1.0, 0.7, 0)
   with a warning line red. The keypad: eleven Item_box cells (32x32, tinted (0.85, 0.85, 0.65),
   (1, 1, 0.8) under the mouse, Inventorybox2 while pressed) at (223 + 40 * (i % 5),
   154 + 38 * (i / 5)), the eleventh the delete key on Back1 / Back2 / Back3; the digits
   (128, 128, 196) and the one under the mouse yellow (196, 196, 0); the digit field a Bar plate
   (40x18) tinted 0.3 at y 134, 16 tall and 52 wide; OK and Cancel at (265, 239) and (343, 239),
   beside the delete key.

   Copied from legacy's generic_confirm_dialog.rcss (a theme sheet replaces the whole file).
   #panel is placed like the 0.97 box (overriding the markup's .center-both); every dimension is
   dp -- the panel carries no transform:scale(root_scale) -- and text is rem (native text size,
   RmlNativeText.h), as legacy does. What legacy has and 0.97 does not (the duel portrait, the
   text field, the progress bar, the live 3D item, a labelled or third button) keeps legacy's
   rule, over the 0.97 box.

   The lines' default colour stays white: generic_confirm_dialog.rml binds every line's colour
   inline ('#ffffff' when the caller gives none) and an inline value outranks this sheet, so the
   0.97 gold needs the markup; a caller's own colour (the red warning line) shows as given. */
#panel {
	/* 0.97: centred horizontally, top edge at y 100, three strips tall (5 + 3 * 40 + 5 = 130;
	   legacy's 117 is the S6 cap and foot) for up to three lines and growing with each further
	   line -- so no centering transform and no fixed height: the flowing .gcd-body below sizes
	   it. y 100 counts from the 640x480 canvas top: the markup adds that canvas's offset
	   (canvas_top, RmlDialogCanvas.h) as margin-top. 213 wide, not legacy's 230: the 0.97 box
	   and its button places are 213 wide, so the edges are Message_box2 itself. */
	top: 100dp;
	left: 50%;
	margin-left: -106.5dp;
	transform: none;
	width: 213dp;
	min-height: 130dp;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
	font-size: 1rem;
	color: token(text-primary);
}
/* Optional taller variant (GenericDialogConfig::tallPanel): the keypad's four-strip box (5 + 4 *
   40 + 5 = 170; legacy's 240) -- the duel portrait sets it too and takes its own size below. The
   bottom-anchored buttons and the edges follow the panel on their own. */
#panel.tall {
	min-height: 170dp;
}
/* The keypad's box: its lines start where 0.97 wrote the title (10 under the top edge, the
   subtitle at 22), and OK and Cancel sit at (265, 239) and (343, 239) -- 52 and 130 from the
   box's left, 10 above its bottom edge -- beside the delete key, whose row ends 8 above that
   edge: the body keeps 2 under the grid (its cells leave 6 more) instead of the button blank.
   The sides keep 6, so the five 40-wide columns fit (200) and the first cell starts 10 from the
   box's left (x 223). 0.97's box is 170 tall with its field at 34 and its cells from 54; here
   the two lines take their own rows, so the box grows past 170 by the same flow as any other.
   The duel portrait, tall as well, takes its own placement back below. */
#panel.tall .gcd-body { margin: 10dp 6dp 2dp 6dp; }
#panel.tall .gcd-btn-primary { left: 52dp; bottom: 10dp; }
#panel.tall .gcd-btn-primary.solo { left: 71dp; }
#panel.tall .gcd-btn-secondary, #panel.tall .gcd-btn-cancel { left: 130dp; bottom: 10dp; }

/* The four sprite layers carry the 0.97 composite: the edges are Message_box2 at its own 213, the
   middle the Message_box1 strips. */
@spritesheet classic-gcd-edge-sheet  { src: ../../../Classic/Message_box2.jpg; classic-gcd-edge: 0px 0px 213px 5px; }
@spritesheet classic-gcd-stone-sheet { src: ../../../Classic/Message_box1.jpg; classic-gcd-stone: 0px 0px 213px 40px; }
.gcd-sprite-back, .gcd-sprite-top, .gcd-sprite-middle, .gcd-sprite-bottom {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	pointer-events: none;
}
/* 0.97 has no backing behind its strips (legacy's newui_msgbox_back): the stone is opaque, so the
   layer stays and draws nothing. */
.gcd-sprite-back { left: 4dp; right: 4dp; top: 5dp; bottom: 5dp; decorator: none; }
.gcd-sprite-top { top: 0; height: 5dp; decorator: image(classic-gcd-edge); }
/* The strips, stacked from the top edge and cut at the bottom one (0.97 drew whole strips; a box
   grown by lines shows part of the last). An atlas sprite repeats as clipped quads inside its
   own rectangle (engine-findings.md, image repeat modes). */
.gcd-sprite-middle { top: 5dp; bottom: 5dp; decorator: image(classic-gcd-stone repeat-y left top); }
.gcd-sprite-bottom { bottom: 0; height: 5dp; decorator: image(classic-gcd-edge); }
/* The overlay-portrait box is the duel request (CDuelMsgBox) and result. 0.97 has no duel; the
   Season 1 client's request (005c8af0) is a 0.97 box at (213, 110), four stones tall
   (5 + 4 * 40 + 5 = 170), its DuelWindow crest (128 x 128) at (256, 120) behind the text, the
   caption bold (255, 207, 24) centred at y 141, the two lines at 180 and 200, each text over a
   black copy one unit down and right, and OK / Cancel (70 x 21) at (237, 250) and (332, 250).
   In the box: the caption at 31, the lines 20 apart ending at 106 (more lines grow upwards), the
   buttons 24 and 119 from its left, 9 above its bottom. */
#panel.portrait {
	top: 110dp;
	min-height: 170dp;
}
#panel.portrait .gcd-body {
	margin: 27dp 6dp 64dp 6dp;
	height: 79dp; /* 170 - 27 top - 64 under the last line */
	align-items: stretch;
}
#panel.portrait .gcd-text-col {
	justify-content: flex-end;
	overflow: visible; /* a fixed native box never scrolls */
}
#panel.portrait .gcd-portrait2d-text { margin-bottom: auto; color: rgb(255, 207, 24); font-effect: shadow(1dp 1dp black); }
/* Positioned so they paint above the (positioned) crest, which comes first in the markup. Regular
   weight unless the caller asks for bold, as Season 1 draws them. */
#panel.portrait .gcd-line {
	position: relative;
	line-height: 20dp;
	min-height: 20dp; /* an empty line keeps its row, as native draws every row at its own y */
	font-weight: normal;
	font-effect: shadow(1dp 1dp black);
}
#panel.portrait .gcd-line.bold { font-weight: bold; }
#panel.portrait .gcd-btn-primary { left: 24dp; bottom: 9dp; }
#panel.portrait .gcd-btn-secondary, #panel.portrait .gcd-btn-cancel { left: 119dp; bottom: 9dp; }

/* GenericDialogConfig::Portrait2D's own art -- the duel crest: Season 1's DuelWindow (128 x 128),
   which Season 1 drew additively (its black square vanishes over the stone): the derived
   DuelWindow_add (tools/classic_theme/make_classic_derived_textures.py) carries that as alpha. */
@spritesheet portrait2d-sheet
{
	src: ../../../Classic/s1/DuelWindow_add.tga;
	portrait2d-image: 0px 0px 128px 128px;
}

/* 0.97 has no title banner (legacy's IMAGE_MSGBOX_TOP_TITLEBAR, newui_Message_03.tga, dropped
   with its @spritesheet): a title is a bold line over the stone, so the rail stays and draws
   nothing, and the title text below stays. */
.gcd-header-rail {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	top: 0;
	height: 67dp;
	pointer-events: none;
	decorator: none;
}
/* Title text over the box -- one centered line rather than native's exact pixel-wrap math -- 10
   under the top edge, where 0.97 centres the keypad's title (y 110). No conflict with
   .gcd-body's own top blank below -- the title sits above that. */
.gcd-header-title {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	top: 10dp;
	text-align: center;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
	font-weight: bold;
	color: token(accent-gold);
	pointer-events: none;
}
.gcd-header-title.warning { color: token(semantic-warning); }
.gcd-header-title.error { color: token(semantic-danger); }

/* Text floats transparently over the stone (painted by the sprite layers above it). 0.97's lines
   start 30 under the top edge (y 130) and its buttons take the bottom 40 (90 from the top, 21
   tall, 19 above the bottom edge): a 30 top blank and a 46 bottom one (the buttons and a 6 gap).
   The sides keep legacy's 184 text column ((213 - 184) / 2 = 14.5), native's wrap width
   (MSGBOX_TEXT_MAXWIDTH 180 plus the renderer's ~2%); the bold 0.97 lines run a little wider, so
   a long line may break one word earlier than in legacy.

   top+bottom (not top+height) deliberately -- this engine's box model is content-box only (no
   box-sizing support anywhere in this codebase), so an explicit height combined with a bordered/
   padded box can push past the intended bottom edge. Anchoring both edges keeps the box's outer
   size exact regardless of its own content.

   display:flex row: #gcd_item3d_anchor (item icon, left) + .gcd-text-col (fills the rest, right).
   The title is NOT a child of this box -- it overlays #panel's own top edge instead. */
.gcd-body {
	/* In flow (not absolute) so the panel grows with it. */
	margin: 30dp 14.5dp 46dp 14.5dp;
	/* Positioned so it paints above the sprite composite, which comes first in the markup. */
	position: relative;
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: row;
	justify-content: center;
	align-items: center;
}
/* Holds lines/input-row/progress-track. Fills .gcd-body's full height explicitly (rather than
   relying on align-items, which wouldn't stretch under align-items:center) so the .scroll-pane
   class it also carries has a real bound to scroll within once content grows taller than the
   panel. The overflow/pointer-events rules and the whole scrollbar chrome now come from
   base.rcss's .scroll-pane -- this element was the case they were generalized from, so only its
   own layout stays here. */
.gcd-text-col {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	justify-content: flex-start;
	align-items: center;
	max-height: 320dp;
	flex: 1 1 auto;
}
/* 0.97 draws the lines bold, 18 apart in the 640x480 frame (y 130, 148, 166: three lines fill the
   130 box, 30 + 3 * 18 + 46). Colour: see the header. */
.gcd-line {
	display: block;
	width: 100%;
	text-align: center;
	white-space: normal;
	line-height: 18dp;
	min-height: 18dp; /* a blank line (" ") keeps its row, as native's AddMsg(L" ") does */
	font-weight: bold;
	color: token(text-primary);
}
.gcd-line.bold { font-weight: bold; }

/* The live 3D item: native C3DItemCommonMsgBox's 40x40 slot (C++ frames the item by this
   element's drawn box: legacy's rule, untouched). */
.gcd-item3d {
	position: relative;
	width: 40dp;
	height: 40dp;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	margin-right: 8dp;
}
/* Collapses when there's no item, so .gcd-text-col alone fills the row. */
.gcd-item3d.hidden { display: none; }
/* The model reaches past its slot, and past the panel, as natively: the image around it is far larger. */
#gcd_item3d { position: absolute; left: -80dp; top: -80dp; width: 200dp; height: 200dp; pointer-events: none; }

/* Optional 2D portrait (GenericDialogConfig::Portrait2D), Overlay layout (the default) -- a direct
   #panel child at Season 1's crest position (y+10, 128x128), behind the text, unlike .gcd-item3d
   (icon-left/text-right, that's the Beside layout below). */
.gcd-portrait2d {
	position: absolute;
	left: 43dp; /* Season 1: 256 - 213 */
	top: 10dp;
	width: 128dp;
	height: 128dp;
	decorator: image(portrait2d-image);
}
/* Same cascade-tie fix as .gcd-item3d above. */
.gcd-portrait2d.hidden { display: none; }
/* Beside layout -- same row-sibling slot/sizing convention as .gcd-item3d, sized a little
   larger since this reads as hero art rather than a small icon. No text overlay in this layout --
   .gcd-portrait2d-text is never a child of this element in the .rml. */
.gcd-portrait2d-beside {
	position: static;
	width: 60dp;
	height: 56dp;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	margin-right: 8dp;
	margin-bottom: 0;
	decorator: image(portrait2d-image);
}
/* The caption row over the crest (native draws it ON TOP of the art): native's bold yellow, first
   row of .gcd-text-col, positioned so it paints above the (positioned) crest. */
.gcd-portrait2d-text {
	position: relative;
	display: block;
	width: 100%;
	line-height: 20dp;
	text-align: center;
	font-weight: bold;
	font-size: 1rem;
	color: token(text-heading);
}
.gcd-portrait2d-text.hidden { display: none; } /* display: block above outranks .hidden */

/* Optional text-entry field -- see the .rml's own comment for the NumericKeypad-vs-Text split.
   `.btn.gcd-keypad-btn`/`.gcd-keypad-delete` override `.btn`'s own `position: absolute` back to
   static so they can flex-wrap into a grid instead of stacking on top of each other. */
@spritesheet classic-gcd-plate-sheet          { src: ../../../Classic/Bar.jpg;           classic-gcd-plate: 0px 0px 40px 18px; }
@spritesheet classic-gcd-cell-sheet           { src: ../../../Classic/Item_box.jpg;      classic-gcd-cell: 0px 0px 32px 32px; }
@spritesheet classic-gcd-cell-pressed-sheet   { src: ../../../Classic/Inventorybox2.jpg; classic-gcd-cell-pressed: 0px 0px 32px 32px; }
@spritesheet classic-gcd-delete-sheet         { src: ../../../Classic/Back1.jpg;         classic-gcd-delete: 0px 0px 32px 32px; }
@spritesheet classic-gcd-delete-hover-sheet   { src: ../../../Classic/Back2.jpg;         classic-gcd-delete-hover: 0px 0px 32px 32px; }
@spritesheet classic-gcd-delete-pressed-sheet { src: ../../../Classic/Back3.jpg;         classic-gcd-delete-pressed: 0px 0px 32px 32px; }
.gcd-input-row {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	align-items: center;
	margin-top: 4dp;
}
/* .gcd-input-row sets its own `display`, so an earlier same-specificity `.hidden { display: none;
   }` (base.rcss) loses the cascade tie without this later, more specific override. */
.gcd-input-row.hidden { display: none; }
/* The digit field: 0.97's Bar plate stretched to 52x16 and tinted 0.3, the digits C++ masks
   centred on it in legacy's prompt colour (0.97's own is not known). */
.gcd-keypad-display {
	width: 52dp;
	height: 16dp;
	line-height: 16dp;
	text-align: center;
	color: token(text-prompt);
	font-weight: bold;
	letter-spacing: 4dp;
	margin-bottom: 4dp;
	decorator: image(classic-gcd-plate fill);
	image-color: #4d4d4d;
}
/* Five 32x32 cells per row, 40 apart, the rows 38 apart (4 at each side of a cell, 6 under it);
   the eleventh, the delete key, starts the third row at the left, where 0.97 draws it beside OK
   and Cancel (#panel.tall above). */
.gcd-keypad-grid {
	display: flex;
	flex-wrap: wrap;
	justify-content: flex-start;
	width: 200dp;
}
.gcd-keypad-grid.hidden { display: none; } /* same cascade-tie fix as .gcd-input-row above */
.btn.gcd-keypad-btn, .btn.gcd-keypad-delete {
	position: static;
	width: 32dp;
	height: 32dp;
	margin: 0 4dp 6dp 4dp;
	line-height: 26dp; /* the digit high in the cell, as 0.97 wrote it at (x + 12, y + 6) */
	font-size: 1rem;
	font-weight: bold;
}
/* The digit cells: Item_box tinted (0.85, 0.85, 0.65), lit (1, 1, 0.8) under the mouse with its
   digit yellow; a pressed one shows the sunk Inventorybox2. */
.btn.gcd-keypad-btn { color: #8080c4; decorator: image(classic-gcd-cell); image-color: #d9d9a6; }
.btn.gcd-keypad-btn:hover { decorator: image(classic-gcd-cell); image-color: #ffffcc; color: #c4c400; }
.btn.gcd-keypad-btn:active { decorator: image(classic-gcd-cell-pressed); image-color: #ffffcc; }
/* The delete key's own art carries its arrow (Back1, Back2 under the mouse, Back3 while pressed),
   so its "Del" label is hidden. */
.btn.gcd-keypad-delete { decorator: image(classic-gcd-delete); color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); }
.btn.gcd-keypad-delete:hover { decorator: image(classic-gcd-delete-hover); }
.btn.gcd-keypad-delete:active { decorator: image(classic-gcd-delete-pressed); }
/* Text-mode field (no 0.97 counterpart in this box: legacy's rule): takes the same flow slot the
   old native-widget position reference occupied, so the column layout is unchanged. Sizing only
   -- fill/border/focus/selection come from base.rcss's shared .text-field. */
.gcd-input-field {
	position: static;
	width: 150dp;
	height: 18dp;
	padding: 0 3dp;
	font-size: 0.85rem;
}

/* Optional progress bar (no 0.97 counterpart in this box: legacy's rule) -- same `x_fraction *
   100 + '%'` fill technique main_frame.rml's own HP/MP/AG/SD/EXP gauges use. */
.gcd-progress-track {
	width: 150dp;
	height: 10dp;
	margin-top: 4dp;
	background-color: token(surface-recessed);
	border: 1dp token(border-inner);
}
.gcd-progress-fill {
	height: 100%;
	background-color: token(accent-gold);
}

/* 0.97's OK / Cancel plates (70x21, the second image under the mouse): paired at 21 and 120 from
   the box's left (x 234 and 333), 90 from its top -- 19 above the bottom edge of the 130 box, so
   they follow the growing panel from the bottom. A lone OK is centred (71, as 0.97's single OK
   at x 284). A button with another label (Decrease / Gift / Discard...; 0.97 has none) gets the
   plain 0.97 plate (Bar, 40x18) stretched to the same size, with its text, as
   message_box_view.rcss does.

   Three fixed, named-role slots (primary/secondary/cancel -- see GenericDialogConfig's own
   comment). `.gcd-btn-secondary` is a real second action (Decrease/Gift/Discard...), never
   Cancel; `.gcd-btn-cancel` is the always-Cancel/Close slot. Every existing Ok/OkCancel consumer
   always renders solo or paired (primary+cancel), never triple. Legacy's newui_button_ok /
   newui_button_cancel sheets are dropped with the S6 art. */
@spritesheet classic-gcd-ok-sheet      { src: ../../../Classic/Ok.jpg;      classic-gcd-ok: 0px 0px 70px 21px; }
@spritesheet classic-gcd-ok2-sheet     { src: ../../../Classic/Ok2.jpg;     classic-gcd-ok-hover: 0px 0px 70px 21px; }
@spritesheet classic-gcd-cancel-sheet  { src: ../../../Classic/Cancel.jpg;  classic-gcd-cancel: 0px 0px 70px 21px; }
@spritesheet classic-gcd-cancel2-sheet { src: ../../../Classic/Cancel2.jpg; classic-gcd-cancel-hover: 0px 0px 70px 21px; }
.btn.gcd-btn-primary, .btn.gcd-btn-secondary, .btn.gcd-btn-cancel {
	bottom: 19dp;
	width: 70dp;
	height: 21dp;
	line-height: 21dp;
	font-size: 1rem;
	color: #ffffff;
	decorator: image(classic-gcd-plate fill);
}
.btn.gcd-btn-primary:hover, .btn.gcd-btn-secondary:hover, .btn.gcd-btn-cancel:hover {
	decorator: image(classic-gcd-plate fill);
	image-color: #ffe6b4;
}
.btn.gcd-btn-primary:active, .btn.gcd-btn-secondary:active, .btn.gcd-btn-cancel:active {
	decorator: image(classic-gcd-plate fill);
	image-color: #b4b4b4;
}
/* The stock OK / Cancel: 0.97's lettered plates, with the label text hidden. */
.btn.gcd-btn-primary.stock-ok { decorator: image(classic-gcd-ok); image-color: #ffffff; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); }
.btn.gcd-btn-primary.stock-ok:hover, .btn.gcd-btn-primary.stock-ok:active { decorator: image(classic-gcd-ok-hover); image-color: #ffffff; }
.btn.gcd-btn-cancel.stock-cancel { decorator: image(classic-gcd-cancel); image-color: #ffffff; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); }
.btn.gcd-btn-cancel.stock-cancel:hover, .btn.gcd-btn-cancel.stock-cancel:active { decorator: image(classic-gcd-cancel-hover); image-color: #ffffff; }
.gcd-btn-primary   { left: 21dp; }
.gcd-btn-primary.solo { left: 71dp; }
/* Paired: whichever of secondary/cancel is the sole second button sits in this one slot -- both
   selectors share the position since only one is ever visible outside of `.triple`. */
.gcd-btn-secondary, .gcd-btn-cancel { left: 120dp; }
/* Triple (all three shown, e.g. Create/Decrease/Cancel; 0.97 has none) -- native's own `triwidth =
   panelWidth/3` centering (CUseFruitCheckMsgBox::SetButtonInfo(), CustomMessageBox.cpp), each
   plate narrowed to 64 and centred within its own 213dp/3 = 71dp third. #panel-qualified so a
   tall or portrait box's paired places above do not override it. */
#panel .gcd-btn-primary.triple { left: 4dp; width: 64dp; }
#panel .gcd-btn-secondary.triple { left: 75dp; width: 64dp; }
#panel .gcd-btn-cancel.triple { left: 146dp; width: 64dp; }

/* Scrolling lists: the Season 1 client's win_scrollbar (as the classic social windows'), in place of
   base.rcss's S6 track and knob: 13x13 arrows at both ends, the track between two 106,97,88 lines,
   a grey thumb sized to the list. */
@spritesheet gcd-scroll-sheet
{
	src: "../../../win_scrollbar.jpg";
	gcd-scroll-thumb: 0px 1px 11px 1px;
	gcd-scroll-up: 0px 3px 13px 13px;
	gcd-scroll-down: 0px 16px 13px 13px;
}
.scroll-pane scrollbarvertical { width: 13dp; margin: 0; }
.scroll-pane scrollbarvertical slidertrack { decorator: none; box-sizing: border-box; border-left: 1dp rgb(106, 97, 88); border-right: 1dp rgb(106, 97, 88); }
.scroll-pane scrollbarvertical sliderbar { height: auto; min-height: 6dp; margin: 0 1dp; decorator: image(gcd-scroll-thumb fill); }
.scroll-pane scrollbarvertical sliderbar:active { filter: none; }
.scroll-pane scrollbarvertical sliderarrowdec,
.scroll-pane scrollbarvertical sliderarrowinc { width: 100%; height: 13dp; pointer-events: auto; }
.scroll-pane scrollbarvertical sliderarrowdec { decorator: image(gcd-scroll-up); }
.scroll-pane scrollbarvertical sliderarrowinc { decorator: image(gcd-scroll-down); }
.scroll-pane scrollbarvertical sliderarrowdec:active,
.scroll-pane scrollbarvertical sliderarrowinc:active { filter: brightness(0.7); }
